{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויהי ביום השמיני קרא משה", :translit "vayehi bayom hashemini kara moshe", :gloss "and it was on the eighth day Moses called"} {:he "היה ביום ראש חדש ניסן", :translit "hayah bayom rosh chodesh nisan", :gloss "it was on the day of the new month of Nisan"} {:he "אמר משה לפי שסרבתי ז' ימים בסנה", :translit "amar moshe mipi shesavarti z' yamim basneh", :gloss "Moses said: because I refused seven days at the bush"} {:he "לכך לא זכיתי לשמש אלא ז'", :translit "lachach lo zachiti lesamesh ela z'", :gloss "therefore I did not merit to minister except seven"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ויהי ביום השמיני קרא משה", :b "היה ביום ראש חדש ניסן"}], :frame {:text "The consecration period for Aaron and his sons as priests lasted seven days, after which their public service began on the eighth day (Leviticus 8:33–9:1). A midrashic tradition identifies this eighth day as the first of Nisan, the day the Tabernacle was erected (Exodus 40:2, 17). Moses served as priest during the seven days of consecration, but Aaron and his sons took over the priesthood on the eighth day (Leviticus 9:1). Moses's reluctance to accept his mission at the Burning Bush for seven days is recorded in Exodus 3:11–4:17.", :sources ["Leviticus 8:33–9:1" "Exodus 40:2" "Exodus 40:17" "Exodus 3:11–4:17"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "ויהי ביום השמיני קרא משה", :a-value 1150, :b "היה ביום ראש חדש ניסן", :b-value 1061, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:34.355027005Z", :model "glm-5.2"}